  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{D}>0 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~b}^2>4 \\mathrm{ac} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{b}=3:(\\mathrm{a}, \\mathrm{c})=(1,1)(1,2)(2,1) \\\\\n& \\mathrm{b}=4:(\\mathrm{a}, \\mathrm{c})=(1,1)(1,2)(2,1)(1,3)(3,1) \\\\\n& \\mathrm{b}=5:(\\mathrm{a}, \\mathrm{c})=(1,1)(1,2)(2,1)(1,3)(3,1)(1,4)(4,1) \\\\\n&(1,5)(5,1)(1,6)(6,1)(2,3)(3,2)(2,2) \\\\\n& \\mathrm{b}=6:(\\mathrm{a}, \\mathrm{c})=(1,1)(1,2)(2,1)(1,3)(3,1)(1,4)(4,1) \\\\\n&(1,5)(5,1)(1,6)(6,1)(2,3)(3,2)(2,4)(4,2)(2,2)\n\\end{aligned}$\nfav. cases $=38$\nProb. : $\\frac{38}{6 \\times 6 \\times 6}$"
